# index.html is generated by the build and rewritten by the build robot every
# time it runs. It must never be merged line by line.
#
# Without this, pulling while you have a local copy of index.html makes git
# stitch the two builds together with conflict markers ("<<<<<<< Updated
# upstream" ... ">>>>>>> Stashed changes"). A browser cannot run that, and the
# whole site goes blank -- which is exactly what happened in September 2026.
#
# -merge tells git to keep one whole version and report the conflict instead of
# writing markers into the file. -diff stops a 5 MB one-line file flooding diffs.
index.html -merge -diff
